WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.873
"Detective Smith is missing," Roxy thought.

2
00:00:03.874 --> 00:00:07.767
"I have to get to police headquarters."

3
00:00:07.768 --> 00:00:11.069
She called to her friends. "Don't wait for me.

4
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:20.069
I, um, dropped something!" Roxy ran off.

5
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.787
*** The parking lot at police headquarters was

6
00:00:23.788 --> 00:00:27.508
empty. "Where are all the police cars?" Roxy

7
00:00:27.509 --> 00:00:33.862
said. "And where is

8
00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:37.734
everyone?" When she went inside, Roxy blinked in

9
00:00:37.735 --> 00:00:42.390
surprise. All the walls were crooked, and the floors were

10
00:00:42.391 --> 00:00:45.643
slanted. "What happened in here?" Roxy

11
00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:49.596
said. "It's like a fun house at an amusement

12
00:00:49.597 --> 00:00:53.260
park!" A hallway was lined with

13
00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:56.661
mirrors. One mirror made Roxy look tall and

14
00:00:56.662 --> 00:01:01.365
skinny. Another one made her head look

15
00:01:01.366 --> 00:01:03.863
enormous. Roxy made her way to the break

16
00:01:03.864 --> 00:01:06.946
room. The coffeemaker was on, and cookies sat on the

17
00:01:06.947 --> 00:01:10.593
counter. Music played on a

18
00:01:10.594 --> 00:01:13.116
radio. But nobody was

19
00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:17.054
there. Roxy scratched her head. "This is

20
00:01:17.055 --> 00:01:19.943
odd." Click . . .

21
00:01:19.944 --> 00:01:24.407
Ba-doom! The floor tilted under Roxy's feet, and she slid down into

22
00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:27.567
darkness. "Oof!" Roxy landed on a hard

23
00:01:27.568 --> 00:01:31.051
floor. "Rocket Girl?" It was Detective

24
00:01:31.052 --> 00:01:35.562
Smith. Using her night vision, Roxy saw she was in a concrete

25
00:01:35.563 --> 00:01:37.384
room. The detective stood near

26
00:01:37.385 --> 00:01:40.428
her. Other police officers were in the room

27
00:01:40.429 --> 00:01:44.327
too. Roxy grinned. "Are you all playing hide-and-seek?"

28
00:01:44.328 --> 00:01:46.315
Detective Smith looked annoyed.

29
00:01:46.316 --> 00:01:50.951
"This isn't funny, Rocket Girl. We've been stuck down here since yesterday!"

30
00:01:50.952 --> 00:01:54.965
Roxy gulped. "Oh . . . Sorry to hear that.

31
00:01:54.966 --> 00:01:59.193
What happened to the building? It's like a fun house."

32
00:01:59.194 --> 00:02:04.048
"We hired a builder to make some improvements." Detective Smith sighed.

33
00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:06.288
"Obviously he did a terrible job.

34
00:02:06.289 --> 00:02:08.758
We can't even use the building now."

35
00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:11.741
"Who is the builder?" Roxy asked.

36
00:02:11.742 --> 00:02:15.105
"His name is Jack Hammer," Detective Smith said.

37
00:02:15.106 --> 00:02:17.183
"We won't hire him again."

38
00:02:17.184 --> 00:02:19.507
Another police officer walked over.

39
00:02:19.508 --> 00:02:23.296
"How will we get out of here?" she asked.

40
00:02:23.297 --> 00:02:27.051
Roxy laughed. "That's easy."

41
00:02:27.052 --> 00:02:34.225
She flew the police officers up to the break room.

42
00:02:34.226 --> 00:02:37.664
Detective Smith grabbed a cookie and took a bite.

43
00:02:37.665 --> 00:02:41.050
The police dispatcher saw a light flashing on the phone.

44
00:02:41.051 --> 00:02:44.556
"Yikes!" she said. "We have messages."

45
00:02:44.557 --> 00:02:47.076
She played the first message.

46
00:02:47.077 --> 00:02:50.808
"Hello? I'm worried about my friends Brenda and Dan Dooley.

47
00:02:50.809 --> 00:02:52.751
They moved into their new house yesterday.

48
00:02:52.752 --> 00:02:54.547
It's at Ten Puddle Lane.

49
00:02:54.548 --> 00:02:59.578
I tried calling and knocking on their door, but there's no answer."

50
00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:02.689
Other people had called with similar messages.

51
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.494
Many of them had called more than once.

52
00:03:05.495 --> 00:03:12.898
Detective Smith swallowed the last bite of his cookie. "Oh boy."

